{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>עיני</b> — The Torah speaks in the language of human beings: \"His eyes\" are His desire and will, or His intellect, which guards men of knowledge from every evil." "<b>ויסלף</b> — HaShem will pervert the words of the traitor who plots evil against men of knowledge, and will annul them."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:09.929563482Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}